The cost of living in Okami — particularly housing — is the highest in Okaiken, and the national minimum wage of approximately 円950 per hour is widely regarded as insufficient to meet basic needs in the city. The poverty rate in Tatara and Minami wards exceeds 25%, while in Aoi and Sakura wards it is below 5%.

===Vital Statistics===
Life expectancy at birth in the Okami metropolitan area is approximately 83.2 years (2025) — significantly above the national average of 80.8 years — reflecting the city's higher average income, better healthcare access, and concentration of medical infrastructure. As with income, life expectancy varies sharply across the wards: Aoi and Sakura have life expectancies above 85 years, while Tatara and Minami have life expectancies below 78 years — a gap of nearly a decade within a single metropolitan area.

